<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4026.18">
  <POU Name="FB_ContainerMoverTests" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000001}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Suite over FB_ContainerMover: the two-axis move, the interlocked hook
    sequence that hands a container over, and everything the shuttle refuses
    before it moves at all.

    It runs against a real FB_StorageLocationMap rather than a stand-in, and
    that is the point of the pairing: the mover asks the map what a location
    holds before it accepts an order, and tells the map what happened only once
    the container is in the rack. A stub map would let both halves of that
    agree with themselves and with nothing else.

    Nothing here advances the clock. The move timeout is real and is asserted,
    but only in FB_ContainerMoverTimingTests, which calls an xStunit intrinsic
    and therefore does not build on the target - everything in THIS file must,
    so nothing here may call it. The cases below reach the timeout's own
    boundary from the outside: with the clock stopped the allowance can never
    elapse, so any number of scans in one state is a state the machine is
    genuinely holding rather than one it is about to time out of.

    The simulated manipulator answers its commands one scan late (see
    ServeManipulator), which is what makes the hook sequence a sequence.  The
    cases about an interlock deliberately do NOT run it: an actuator that never
    reports itself is exactly what an interlock is there to stand in front of.
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_ContainerMoverTests EXTENDS TcUnit.FB_TestSuite]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[AFreshMoverIsIdleAndHoldsNoOrder();
AnOrderHomesTheShuttleBeforeItTravels();
BothAxesAreCommandedTogetherRatherThanOneAfterTheOther();
TheAxisTargetsAreReadFromTheSurveyedPositionTable();
TheHookReachTakesItsSignFromTheRackFace();
AStoreOrderRunsTheHookSequenceAndTellsTheMapOnlyOnceItIsDone();
ARetrieveOrderReturnsTheLocationToTheFreePool();
TheHooksMayNotReachIntoTheRackUntilTheyAreHome();
TheHooksMayNotReachIntoTheRackUntilTheCylinderIsSet();
TheOrderIsNotCompleteUntilTheHooksAreBackFromTheRack();
AnOrderForALocationTheRackingDoesNotHaveIsFaulted();
AnOrderForAnotherAislesRackIsFaulted();
StoringIntoALocationNobodyReservedIsFaulted();
RetrievingFromAnEmptyLocationIsFaulted();
ATargetOutsideTheAxisEnvelopeIsFaulted();
AnOrderArrivingWhileTheShuttleIsBusyIsRefusedWithoutFaulting();
ADriveFaultLatchesUntilItIsAcknowledged();
TheCoordinatedMoveReportsTheLongerOfItsTwoLegsAsRemaining();]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Method Name="AFreshMoverIsIdleAndHoldsNoOrder" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000002}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// A shuttle that has been scanned but never ordered anywhere must not claim a
// reference it has not established. A mover that powered up believing itself
// homed would take its first order straight into the racking from wherever the
// last shift left it.
METHOD PRIVATE AFreshMoverIsIdleAndHoldsNoOrder
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AFreshMoverIsIdleAndHoldsNoOrder');

Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.IDLE,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a mover that has not been ordered anywhere');

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Homed, Message := 'a mover claimed a reference it never established');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Busy, Message := 'a mover with no order reported itself busy');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Fault, Message := 'a fresh mover reported a fault');

AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 0, Actual := mover.ErrorID, Message := 'ErrorID with nothing wrong');
AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 0, Actual := mover.TargetIndex, Message := 'TargetIndex with no order');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AnOrderHomesTheShuttleBeforeItTravels" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000003}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The first order after a power-up establishes the reference before it uses
// it. Travelling first and homing later would mean the very first move is the
// one made from an unknown position, which is the move most likely to end
// inside a rack upright.
METHOD PRIVATE AnOrderHomesTheShuttleBeforeItTravels
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AnOrderHomesTheShuttleBeforeItTravels');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

AssertTrue(Condition := mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153,
                                             Barcode := 'C-000153',
                                             StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00),
           Message := 'a store order for a reserved location was refused');

Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.HOMING,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the first order did not home the shuttle first');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Homed, Message := 'the shuttle was homed before it had finished homing');
AssertTrue(Condition := mover.Busy, Message := 'a shuttle on its way to a location reported itself free');

Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertTrue(Condition := mover.Homed, Message := 'reaching the home reference did not establish it');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.MOVE_HORIZONTAL,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the shuttle did not set off once it was homed');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="BothAxesAreCommandedTogetherRatherThanOneAfterTheOther" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000004}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The move is coordinated: MOVE_HORIZONTAL and MOVE_VERTICAL name the axis
// still outstanding, not two legs run one after the other. The mast has its
// target from the first scan of the travel and can - and here does - arrive
// while the rail is still going.
//
// A shuttle that ran its legs in sequence would take the SUM of the two on
// every order instead of the longer of them. Nothing about the state names
// would change, which is why this is asserted on the mast's commanded position
// rather than on the state.
METHOD PRIVATE BothAxesAreCommandedTogetherRatherThanOneAfterTheOther
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('BothAxesAreCommandedTogetherRatherThanOneAfterTheOther');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);
mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.MOVE_HORIZONTAL),
           Message := 'the shuttle never set off');

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 6253.5,
                   Actual := liftAxis.CommandedPosition,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the mast was left without a target while the rail travelled');

// The mast has the shorter leg by some 9.5 metres, so it finishes first - with
// the rail still travelling and the state still naming the rail.
ScanTimes(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Count := 13);

AssertTrue(Condition := liftAxis.InPosition,
           Message := 'the mast had not arrived after enough scans to cover its leg twice over');
AssertFalse(Condition := railAxis.InPosition, Message := 'the rail finished its far longer leg first');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.MOVE_HORIZONTAL,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the mast arriving ended the travel while the rail was still going');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TheAxisTargetsAreReadFromTheSurveyedPositionTable" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000005}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Both targets come out of the surveyed table, and the two locations chosen
// here are what makes that assertable: position 13 and level 8 are the two
// entries that do NOT sit on the nominal pitch, so a mover computing its
// targets from a pitch and an offset lands 4.5 mm and 3.5 mm out - further
// than the in-position window, which is a container set down on the edge of a
// shelf. The second order is on the pitch, so a table read backwards or offset
// by one would still be caught.
METHOD PRIVATE TheAxisTargetsAreReadFromTheSurveyedPositionTable
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('TheAxisTargetsAreReadFromTheSurveyedPositionTable');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 7, Position := 12);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 15804.5,
                   Actual := mover.RailTarget,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the rail target of the position surveyed off the pitch');
AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 6253.5,
                   Actual := mover.LiftTarget,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the mast target of the level surveyed off the pitch');
AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 153, Actual := mover.TargetIndex, Message := 'the location the order named');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.AT_TARGET),
           Message := 'the first order never finished');

mover.StoreContainer(Index := 132, Barcode := 'C-000132', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:30:00);

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 14550.0,
                   Actual := mover.RailTarget,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the rail target of a position on the nominal pitch');
AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 5400.0,
                   Actual := mover.LiftTarget,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the mast target of a level on the nominal pitch');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TheHookReachTakesItsSignFromTheRackFace" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000006}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// One rail serves the rack on either side of it, so the two faces of an aisle
// share a rail position entirely and differ only in the direction the hooks
// reach. Losing the sign would send every second container into the rack
// opposite the one the MES allocated - and the shuttle would report the move
// as complete, because everything except the reach was right.
METHOD PRIVATE TheHookReachTakesItsSignFromTheRackFace
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('TheHookReachTakesItsSignFromTheRackFace');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 2, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := -780.0,
                   Actual := mover.HookReach,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the reach into the near rack face');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.AT_TARGET),
           Message := 'the near-face order never finished');

mover.StoreContainer(Index := 453, Barcode := 'C-000453', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:30:00);

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 780.0,
                   Actual := mover.HookReach,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the reach into the far rack face');

// The far face is the same distance along the same rail at the same height -
// the sign of the reach is the whole of the difference between the two.
AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 15804.5,
                   Actual := mover.RailTarget,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the far face moved the rail target');
AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 6253.5,
                   Actual := mover.LiftTarget,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the far face moved the mast target');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AStoreOrderRunsTheHookSequenceAndTellsTheMapOnlyOnceItIsDone" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000007}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// A store end to end, and the property the whole sequence exists to protect:
// the map is not told anything until the container is somewhere it will stay
// if the machine stops. A mover that marked the location occupied when it
// accepted the order, or when it arrived, would leave the warehouse holding a
// container that is still on the shuttle deck - and a retrieval order for it
// would send the shuttle to an empty shelf.
//
// The cylinder stroke is asserted in both directions because it is the one
// thing that flips: a store approaches with the container carried above shelf
// height and sets it down, which is the opposite of what a retrieval does with
// the same two actuators.
METHOD PRIVATE AStoreOrderRunsTheHookSequenceAndTellsTheMapOnlyOnceItIsDone
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AStoreOrderRunsTheHookSequenceAndTellsTheMapOnlyOnceItIsDone');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);
mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.HOOKS_ENGAGING),
           Message := 'the shuttle never reached the rack face');
AssertTrue(Condition := mover.EngageHooks, Message := 'the hooks were not commanded out');
AssertTrue(Condition := mover.RaiseCylinder, Message := 'a store approached with the container already down');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.RESERVED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the map was written before the hooks had even reached');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.LIFTING),
           Message := 'the hooks never latched the container');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.RaiseCylinder, Message := 'the transfer stroke did not set the container down');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.RESERVED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the map was written mid-transfer');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.HOOKS_RELEASING),
           Message := 'the cylinder never completed its stroke');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.EngageHooks, Message := 'the hooks were still commanded out while letting go');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.RESERVED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the map was written while the hooks were still in the rack');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.AT_TARGET),
           Message := 'the hooks never came home');

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.OCCUPIED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the completed store never reached the map');
AssertEquals_STRING(Expected := 'C-000153',
                    Actual := map.BarcodeAt(Index := 153),
                    Message := 'the barcode the order carried');
AssertEquals_DATE_AND_TIME(Expected := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00,
                           Actual := map.StoredTimeAt(Index := 153),
                           Message := 'the time the order carried');
AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 1, Actual := map.OccupiedCount, Message := 'OccupiedCount after the store');
AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 1, Actual := map.StoredTotal, Message := 'StoredTotal after the store');

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Busy, Message := 'a finished shuttle still reported an order in flight');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Fault, Message := 'a completed store faulted');
AssertTrue(Condition := mover.Homed, Message := 'a completed order cost the shuttle its reference');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ARetrieveOrderReturnsTheLocationToTheFreePool" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000008}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The other half of the warehouse, and the same three actuators run the other
// way round: the hooks come in UNDER a container on a shelf and the cylinder
// lifts it off. The location goes back to the free pool with the container's
// details cleared off it, because a barcode left on an empty shelf is what a
// later retrieval order chases after a container that has already shipped.
METHOD PRIVATE ARetrieveOrderReturnsTheLocationToTheFreePool
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ARetrieveOrderReturnsTheLocationToTheFreePool');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
map.Store(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

AssertTrue(Condition := mover.RetrieveContainer(Index := 153),
           Message := 'a retrieval order for an occupied location was refused');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.HOOKS_ENGAGING),
           Message := 'the shuttle never reached the rack face');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.RaiseCylinder,
            Message := 'a retrieval approached with the hooks already up, above the container it came for');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.LIFTING),
           Message := 'the hooks never latched the container');
AssertTrue(Condition := mover.RaiseCylinder,
           Message := 'the transfer stroke did not take the container off its shelf');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.OCCUPIED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the map was told the container had gone mid-transfer');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.AT_TARGET),
           Message := 'the retrieval never finished');

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.FREE,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the emptied location never went back to the free pool');
AssertEquals_STRING(Expected := '',
                    Actual := map.BarcodeAt(Index := 153),
                    Message := 'the barcode of a container that has left the warehouse');
AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 1800, Actual := map.FreeCount, Message := 'FreeCount after the retrieval');
AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 0, Actual := map.OccupiedCount, Message := 'OccupiedCount after the retrieval');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TheHooksMayNotReachIntoTheRackUntilTheyAreHome" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000009}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Hooks that never reported themselves home hold the sequence at the end of
// the travel however long the shuttle stands there. HooksReleased is its own
// sensor rather than NOT HooksEngaged precisely so that a manipulator stopped
// half way out reads as neither, and this is the interlock that reads it.
METHOD PRIVATE TheHooksMayNotReachIntoTheRackUntilTheyAreHome
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('TheHooksMayNotReachIntoTheRackUntilTheyAreHome');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

// A shuttle carrying a container, with its hooks stopped somewhere between
// engaged and home.
mover.HooksReleased := FALSE;
mover.CylinderRaised := TRUE;
mover.CylinderLowered := FALSE;

mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);
ScanTimes(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Count := 60);

AssertTrue(Condition := railAxis.InPosition, Message := 'the rail never arrived');
AssertTrue(Condition := liftAxis.InPosition, Message := 'the mast never arrived');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.MOVE_VERTICAL,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the hooks reached into the rack without ever having come home');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.EngageHooks, Message := 'the hooks were commanded out past the interlock');

mover.HooksReleased := TRUE;
Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.HOOKS_ENGAGING,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the hooks did not reach once they reported themselves home');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TheHooksMayNotReachIntoTheRackUntilTheCylinderIsSet" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-00000000000a}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The second half of the same interlock. A store is carrying its container
// above shelf height, so the cylinder has to be up before the hooks push it
// in; with the cylinder still down the container would be driven into the
// shelf edge rather than over it.
METHOD PRIVATE TheHooksMayNotReachIntoTheRackUntilTheCylinderIsSet
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('TheHooksMayNotReachIntoTheRackUntilTheCylinderIsSet');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
// Arrange leaves the shuttle at rest with its cylinder down, which is the
// wrong end for a store.
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);
AssertTrue(Condition := mover.RaiseCylinder, Message := 'a store did not command the approach stroke');

ScanTimes(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Count := 60);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.MOVE_VERTICAL,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the hooks pushed a container in with the cylinder still down');

mover.CylinderRaised := TRUE;
mover.CylinderLowered := FALSE;
Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.HOOKS_ENGAGING,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the hooks did not reach once the cylinder had made its approach stroke');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TheOrderIsNotCompleteUntilTheHooksAreBackFromTheRack" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-00000000000b}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The last interlock in the sequence, and the one that decides when the map is
// written. A shuttle that called the order done with its hooks still out would
// be free to accept the next order and set off along the rail with a hook
// inside a rack face.
METHOD PRIVATE TheOrderIsNotCompleteUntilTheHooksAreBackFromTheRack
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('TheOrderIsNotCompleteUntilTheHooksAreBackFromTheRack');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);
mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.HOOKS_RELEASING),
           Message := 'the transfer never reached the point of letting go');

// From here the manipulator is left unattended, so the hooks never report
// themselves home.
ScanTimes(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Count := 20);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.HOOKS_RELEASING,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the order completed with the hooks still in the rack');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.RESERVED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the map was written while the hooks were still in the rack');
AssertTrue(Condition := mover.Busy, Message := 'a shuttle with a hook still out reported itself free');

mover.HooksReleased := TRUE;
Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.AT_TARGET,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the hooks coming home did not finish the order');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.OCCUPIED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the finished order never reached the map');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AnOrderForALocationTheRackingDoesNotHaveIsFaulted" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-00000000000c}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// An index the map cannot resolve is a MES and a PLC that disagree about how
// big the warehouse is. It is refused before the shuttle moves, and it is a
// FAULT rather than a quiet refusal: a machine that silently declined those
// would keep taking orders while the disagreement got worse, and the container
// on its deck would have nowhere to go either way.
METHOD PRIVATE AnOrderForALocationTheRackingDoesNotHaveIsFaulted
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AnOrderForALocationTheRackingDoesNotHaveIsFaulted');

Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.StoreContainer(Index := 1801,
                                              Barcode := 'C-000000',
                                              StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00),
            Message := 'an order past the last location of the racking was accepted');

Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertTrue(Condition := mover.Fault, Message := 'an order the racking cannot serve did not fault the shuttle');
AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 16#85010002,
                   Actual := mover.ErrorID,
                   Message := 'ErrorID for a location outside the racking');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.FAULT,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'state after an order the racking cannot serve');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Busy, Message := 'a faulted shuttle reported an order in flight');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AnOrderForAnotherAislesRackIsFaulted" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-00000000000d}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// A shuttle runs on one rail in one aisle and physically cannot reach the
// others, so an order for aisle two is another shuttle's work. The location is
// perfectly valid, which is the point: nothing about the index says it is out
// of reach, only the recipe does.
METHOD PRIVATE AnOrderForAnotherAislesRackIsFaulted
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AnOrderForAnotherAislesRackIsFaulted');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 2, Side := 1, Level := 1, Position := 1);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.StoreContainer(Index := 601,
                                              Barcode := 'C-000601',
                                              StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00),
            Message := 'the aisle-one shuttle accepted an order in aisle two');

Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 16#85010003,
                   Actual := mover.ErrorID,
                   Message := 'ErrorID for a location in another aisle');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.RESERVED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 601),
                 Message := 'the refused order disturbed the location it named');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="StoringIntoALocationNobodyReservedIsFaulted" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-00000000000e}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The map is asked what a location holds BEFORE the shuttle sets off, and a
// store may only go to one that was set aside for it. Storing into a free
// location would mean the container arrived somewhere the allocator can hand
// out from under it, and the next order would send a second container to the
// same shelf.
METHOD PRIVATE StoringIntoALocationNobodyReservedIsFaulted
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('StoringIntoALocationNobodyReservedIsFaulted');

Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153,
                                              Barcode := 'C-000153',
                                              StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00),
            Message := 'a store into a location nobody reserved was accepted');

Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 16#85010004,
                   Actual := mover.ErrorID,
                   Message := 'ErrorID for a store into an unreserved location');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.FREE,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the refused store wrote to the map anyway');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="RetrievingFromAnEmptyLocationIsFaulted" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-00000000000f}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The mirror of the store check, and it asks the map for the opposite answer.
// A shuttle sent after a container that is not there would come back empty and
// report success, and the container the order was really about would stay
// wherever it is with nothing looking for it.
METHOD PRIVATE RetrievingFromAnEmptyLocationIsFaulted
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('RetrievingFromAnEmptyLocationIsFaulted');

// Reserved, not free: a location that has been allocated still has nothing in
// it, and a retrieval that accepted one would race the container on its way.
map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.RetrieveContainer(Index := 153),
            Message := 'a retrieval from a location holding nothing was accepted');

Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 16#85010005,
                   Actual := mover.ErrorID,
                   Message := 'ErrorID for a retrieval from an empty location');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.FAULT,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'state after a retrieval from an empty location');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ATargetOutsideTheAxisEnvelopeIsFaulted" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000010}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// A surveyed position beyond the travel the shuttle physically has means the
// rack model and the machine no longer describe each other - a rack extended
// without the survey being redone, or a shuttle swapped for a shorter one. The
// check is on the way in rather than on the axis, because an axis refusing a
// move it has already started is too late to stop it reaching its end stop.
METHOD PRIVATE ATargetOutsideTheAxisEnvelopeIsFaulted
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ATargetOutsideTheAxisEnvelopeIsFaulted');

// A rail that stops short of the far half of the aisle.
recipe.PositionReferences.RailMaximum := 15000.0;

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153,
                                              Barcode := 'C-000153',
                                              StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00),
            Message := 'an order beyond the end of the rail was accepted');

Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 16#85010006,
                   Actual := mover.ErrorID,
                   Message := 'ErrorID for a target outside the travel the shuttle has');
AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 0.0,
                   Actual := railAxis.CommandedPosition,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the rail was commanded past its own end stop');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AnOrderArrivingWhileTheShuttleIsBusyIsRefusedWithoutFaulting" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000011}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The one refusal that is NOT a fault. A second order arriving mid-move is
// ordinary flow control - the unit above simply re-offers it when the shuttle
// is free - and faulting on it would stop a machine that has nothing wrong
// with it every time two orders landed close together.
METHOD PRIVATE AnOrderArrivingWhileTheShuttleIsBusyIsRefusedWithoutFaulting
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AnOrderArrivingWhileTheShuttleIsBusyIsRefusedWithoutFaulting');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 14);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);

mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);
ScanTimes(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Count := 4);

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.StoreContainer(Index := 154,
                                              Barcode := 'C-000154',
                                              StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:05:00),
            Message := 'a second order was accepted on top of one in flight');

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Fault, Message := 'a second order faulted a shuttle that was working normally');
AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 0, Actual := mover.ErrorID, Message := 'ErrorID after a refused second order');
AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 153,
                  Actual := mover.TargetIndex,
                  Message := 'the refused order took over the one in flight');

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.AT_TARGET),
           Message := 'the order in flight did not survive the refusal');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.OCCUPIED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the order in flight never reached the map');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.RESERVED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 154),
                 Message := 'the refused order reached the map anyway');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ADriveFaultLatchesUntilItIsAcknowledged" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000012}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The latch is the whole point: a drive drops its error the moment the cause
// goes away, and a shuttle that resumed a move on that would be a machine that
// restarts by itself with a container half way into a rack face. The fault
// outlives its cause and is cleared by a person, not by the drive.
//
// The reference goes with it. A shuttle cannot know what moved while it was
// faulted, so the next order re-homes before it travels - which is asserted
// here rather than assumed, because a mover that kept Homed through a fault
// would look identical until the first time an axis really had slipped.
METHOD PRIVATE ADriveFaultLatchesUntilItIsAcknowledged
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ADriveFaultLatchesUntilItIsAcknowledged');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);
mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);
ScanTimes(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Count := 4);

railAxis.DriveFault := TRUE;
Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertTrue(Condition := mover.Fault, Message := 'a tripped drive did not fault the shuttle');
AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 16#85010007,
                   Actual := mover.ErrorID,
                   Message := 'ErrorID for a drive fault');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.FAULT,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'state after a drive fault');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Homed, Message := 'a faulted shuttle kept a reference it can no longer trust');
AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Busy, Message := 'a faulted shuttle still reported an order in flight');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_LocationState.RESERVED,
                 Actual := map.StateAt(Index := 153),
                 Message := 'the abandoned order wrote to the map on its way out');

// The cause goes away on its own, which the machine must not treat as an
// acknowledgement.
railAxis.DriveFault := FALSE;
ScanTimes(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Count := 5);

AssertTrue(Condition := mover.Fault, Message := 'the fault cleared itself when its cause went away');
AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 16#85010007,
                   Actual := mover.ErrorID,
                   Message := 'ErrorID while the fault is still standing');

mover.Reset := TRUE;
Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);
mover.Reset := FALSE;

AssertFalse(Condition := mover.Fault, Message := 'the acknowledgement did not release the latch');
AssertEquals_UDINT(Expected := 0, Actual := mover.ErrorID, Message := 'ErrorID after the acknowledgement');
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.IDLE,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'state after the acknowledgement');

AssertTrue(Condition := mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153,
                                             Barcode := 'C-000153',
                                             StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-07:00:00),
           Message := 'an acknowledged shuttle refused the order again');

Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_MoverState.HOMING,
                 Actual := mover.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the shuttle set off again without re-establishing its reference');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TheCoordinatedMoveReportsTheLongerOfItsTwoLegsAsRemaining" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000013}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// TravelRemaining is what a coordinated move has left, which is the longer of
// the two legs and not their sum: the axes run at the same time, so the move
// is over when the one with furthest to go arrives. Adding them would nearly
// double every estimate the shuttle publishes, and the numbers here are chosen
// so that the sum, the shorter leg and the longer leg are three different
// answers.
METHOD PRIVATE TheCoordinatedMoveReportsTheLongerOfItsTwoLegsAsRemaining
VAR
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('TheCoordinatedMoveReportsTheLongerOfItsTwoLegsAsRemaining');

map.Reserve(Aisle := 1, Side := 1, Level := 8, Position := 13);
Arrange(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, recipe := recipe);
mover.StoreContainer(Index := 153, Barcode := 'C-000153', StoredAt := DT#2026-08-05-06:00:00);

AssertTrue(Condition := RunUntil(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis,
                                 Target := E_MoverState.MOVE_HORIZONTAL),
           Message := 'the shuttle never set off');

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 15804.5,
                   Actual := mover.TravelRemaining,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the travel a move of 15804.5 mm and 6253.5 mm still has to run');

// Thirteen scans at 500 mm each puts the mast exactly on its target and leaves
// the rail at 6500 mm.
ScanTimes(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Count := 13);

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 6253.5,
                   Actual := liftAxis.ActualPosition,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the mast overshot its target on its last step');
AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 9304.5,
                   Actual := mover.TravelRemaining,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the travel remaining once the shorter leg has finished');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Arrange" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000014}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Puts a shuttle in the state one is found in at the start of a shift: at
// rest at the aisle end, hooks home, cylinder down, nothing on the deck, and
// its map bound.
//
// The map is bound by CALLING the mover, not by writing a field, because it is
// a VAR_IN_OUT: it has to travel on every invocation, and this is the one that
// establishes it before the first order method reads it.
//
// The caller sets any recipe field it cares about BEFORE calling this.
METHOD PRIVATE Arrange
VAR_IN_OUT
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
	recipe : ST_MoverControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[mover.HooksReleased := TRUE;
mover.HooksEngaged := FALSE;
mover.CylinderLowered := TRUE;
mover.CylinderRaised := FALSE;

railAxis();
liftAxis();
mover(railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis, Control := recipe, locationMap := map);]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Scan" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000015}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// One PLC scan of the whole run, in the order a real task would: the control
// modules first, so the equipment module reads a world that has already
// answered its previous commands, and never the other way round.
//
// Only the map is re-supplied. The axes are interface inputs and hold the
// reference Arrange gave them, but a VAR_IN_OUT has to be passed on every
// call.
METHOD PRIVATE Scan
VAR_IN_OUT
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[railAxis();
liftAxis();
mover(locationMap := map);]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ScanTimes" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000016}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Runs the shuttle for a fixed number of scans with the manipulator left
// unattended, so the hooks and the cylinder report whatever the case last set
// them to. That is what makes an interlock observable: an actuator that never
// answers is exactly the thing an interlock stands in front of.
METHOD PRIVATE ScanTimes
VAR_IN_OUT
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
	Count : UINT;
END_VAR
VAR
	i : UINT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[FOR i := 1 TO Count DO
	Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);
END_FOR]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ServeManipulator" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000017}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The hook and cylinder control modules answering the commands they were given
// on the previous scan.
//
// One scan of lag, and it is what makes the hook sequence a sequence rather
// than a single cycle: every step in it waits on an actuator that only reports
// itself after the mover has asked. Instant feedback would collapse all three
// transfer states into one scan and the ordering between them would stop being
// observable at all.
METHOD PRIVATE ServeManipulator
VAR_IN_OUT
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[mover.HooksEngaged := mover.EngageHooks;
mover.HooksReleased := NOT mover.EngageHooks;
mover.CylinderRaised := mover.RaiseCylinder;
mover.CylinderLowered := NOT mover.RaiseCylinder;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="RunUntil" Id="{5e4501d0-0037-4d19-9a41-000000000018}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Scans the run, with the manipulator answering, until the shuttle reaches
// Target. FALSE if it faulted or never got there.
//
// Returning a verdict rather than simply stopping is what keeps a case honest:
// a run that never arrived would otherwise leave the assertions below it
// reading whatever state the loop gave up in, and several of them would still
// pass.
METHOD PRIVATE RunUntil : BOOL
VAR_IN_OUT
	mover : FB_ContainerMover;
	map : FB_StorageLocationMap;
	railAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
	liftAxis : FB_PositioningAxis;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
	Target : E_MoverState;
END_VAR
VAR
	guard : UINT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[RunUntil := FALSE;

// The bound is far above the ~40 scans the longest move in this suite takes,
// and exists only so a machine that stopped advancing ends the case instead of
// the run.
FOR guard := 1 TO 400 DO
	IF mover.CurrentState = Target THEN
		RunUntil := TRUE;
		EXIT;
	END_IF

	IF mover.Fault THEN
		EXIT;
	END_IF

	ServeManipulator(mover := mover);
	Scan(mover := mover, map := map, railAxis := railAxis, liftAxis := liftAxis);
END_FOR]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>
